==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|collaret}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|collerette}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kɒləˈɹɛt/|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[collar]], especially as a kind of [[necklace]] of lace, fur etc. for women; a [[ruff]]
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Weldon's Practical Needlework |author=| page=70| passage=Work the 2 stitches in looped knitting; the last ten rows make a kind of gore on the lower edge of the '''collarette'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022| title=The Heretic|author=Liam McIlvanney| page=206| passage=Men in Sunday suits and orange '''collarettes''' swaggered to the music from uniformed flute bands.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023| title=Freemasonic Enlightenment in the Context of the Modern and Perfecting Rite of Symbolic Masonry|author=Nicolas Laos | page=226| passage=The regalia of the Regional Grand Officers comprise the following items: an apron, a sash, a pair of gauntlets, a cap, a '''collarette''', a collarette jewel, and the Order's breast jewel. }}
# A small collar of inner petals or leaf-like extensions to the stem.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1917| title=Name this Flower|author=Gaston Bonnier | page=226| passage=There are no recurved strap-shaped little flowers; '''collarette''' of the composite flower with scales arranged in several rows ( Fig . TVU ) }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Biology of Conidial Fungi |author=Garry T. Cole | page=301| passage=The rather inconspicuous '''collarette''' of Aspergillus contrasts with the distinctive '''collarette''' of Phialophora richardsiae (Nannf. apud Melin & Nannf.) }}
# A type of [[dahlia]] having a small collar of short inner petals.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914| title=The Standard Cyclopedia of Horticulture|author=Liberty Hyde Bailey | page=956| passage=The '''Collarette''' dahlia is a very novel and distinct type.}}
# The jagged circle in the mid-diameter of the [[iris]], separating the darker shade of the iris from the lighter shade of the iris.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015| title=Clinical Ocular Prosthetics |author=Keith R. Pine; Brian H. Sloan; Robert J. Jacobs | page=129| passage=The edge of the pupil is soft and seems to dissolve into the '''collarette''' rather than stand apart from it. }}
# The rim of loosened [[keratin]] surrounding a [[skin]] [[lesion]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021| title=Pediatric Dermoscopy Trichoscopy & Onychoscopy |author=Subrata Malakar | page=35| passage=Occasionally, scaling may be diffuse and irregular instead of '''collarette''' of fragments of scales that from the border into the center of the lesion, like a curtain}}
# {{lb|en|advertising}} An [[advertising]] [[card]] fitted around the [[neck]] of a [[bottle]].

